  "//levels": "The field is a function of `level`: the goal walks a circle, the two magnets take positions from a different-period trig so the field geometry changes every level, and the ball starts opposite the goal. `curLvl` drives `rebuild`; death sets curLvl to -1 to rebuild the same level.",
  "//geometry": "Everything sits on a common circle at fixed angular offsets, rotated by level: magnets at t and t+pi, goal and ball at t+pi/2 and t-pi/2. Independent trig per entity does not guarantee separation - it put the ball inside a magnet at level 1."
}
